      {
        "title": "Test Coverage Analysis — Canon (`F:\\canon\\web`)",
        "content": "\n**Baseline: 0% coverage.** No test files exist anywhere in the repo, and no test runner is installed (`package.json` has no `jest`/`vitest`/`playwright`, no `test` script). This is a from-scratch setup, not a gap-filling exercise. I read every file under `lib/`, `types/`, `app/api/`, and the one custom hook to build this.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "0. Prerequisite: install a test runner",
        "content": "\nNothing below can run until this exists. Recommended: **Vitest** (native ESM/TS, fast, trivial `@/*` alias mapping) + `@testing-library/react` for the one hook, plus **Playwright** for the auth-gated E2E flows (you already have the `playwright-cli` skill available).\n\n```json\n// package.json additions\n\"devDependencies\": {\n  \"vitest\": \"^3\",\n  \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^5\",\n  \"@testing-library/react\": \"^16\",\n  \"jsdom\": \"^25\"\n},\n\"scripts\": {\n  \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n  \"test:watch\": \"vitest\"\n}\n```\n\n```ts\n// vitest.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\nimport path from \"path\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  test: { environment: \"node\", include: [\"**/*.test.ts\", \"**/*.test.tsx\"] },\n  resolve: { alias: { \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \".\") } },\n});\n```\n\nComponent-level tests (`use-review.ts`) need `environment: \"jsdom\"` — either a second config or per-file `// @vitest-environment jsdom` pragma.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "1. Pure functions — highest ROI, zero mocking needed",
        "content": "\nThese are pure, deterministic, and currently **100% untested**.\n\n**`lib/diff-chars.ts` → `diffSegments`**\n```ts\n// lib/diff-chars.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { diffSegments } from \"@/lib/diff-chars\";\n\ndescribe(\"diffSegments\", () => {\n  it(\"returns whole value as prefix when strings are equal\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n  it(\"finds a differing suffix (APAC vs APAC-SOUTH)\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC-SOUTH\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n  it(\"finds a differing middle with shared prefix and suffix\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"ACC-\", middle: \"4417\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n  it(\"handles totally disjoint strings\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"Acme Inc.\", \"ACME INC\")).toBeDefined(); // no shared prefix/suffix expected\n  });\n  it(\"handles empty strings on either side\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"\", \"ACME\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n    expect(diffSegments(\"ACME\", \"\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n  it(\"does not let overlapping prefix/suffix double-count on repeated chars (aaa vs aa)\", () => {\n    // regression guard for the max-min bound in the suffix loop\n    const result = diffSegments(\"aaa\", \"aa\");\n    expect(result.prefix.length + result.middle.length + result.suffix.length).toBe(3);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/format.ts`** — 8 exported functions, none tested.\n```ts\n// lib/format.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  shortRunId, formatElapsed, formatCount, formatStat,\n  formatClockTime, formatTimestamp, formatRelative, formatConfidence,\n} from \"@/lib/format\";\n\ndescribe(\"shortRunId\", () => {\n  it(\"strips hyphens and formats as 4·2\", () => {\n    expect(shortRunId(\"a41fc9d2-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\")).toBe(\"a41f·c9\");\n  });\n  it(\"does not throw on a short/malformed id\", () => {\n    expect(() => shortRunId(\"ab\")).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatElapsed\", () => {\n  it.each([\n    [0, \"00:00\"], [59_000, \"00:59\"], [60_000, \"01:00\"],\n    [3_661_000, \"1:01:01\"], [-500, \"00:00\"], // negative clamps to 0 — edge case, unverified intent\n  ])(\"%i ms -> %s\", (ms, expected) => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(ms)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatCount / formatStat\", () => {\n  it(\"adds thousands separators\", () => expect(formatCount(12345)).toBe(\"12,345\"));\n  it(\"renders em dash for null/undefined, not zero\", () => {\n    expect(formatStat(null)).toBe(\"—\");\n    expect(formatStat(undefined)).toBe(\"—\");\n    expect(formatStat(0)).toBe(\"0\"); // must NOT collapse to the em dash\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatRelative\", () => {\n  const now = new Date(\"2026-08-08T12:00:00Z\");\n  it.each([\n    [30_000, \"just now\"], [90_000, \"2m ago\"],\n    [2 * 3600_000, \"2h ago\"], [3 * 86_400_000, \"3d ago\"],\n  ])(\"%i ms ago\", (deltaMs, expected) => {\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(now.getTime() - deltaMs), now)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n  it(\"does not go negative for a future date (clock skew)\", () => {\n    expect(() => formatRelative(new Date(now.getTime() + 5000), now)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatConfidence\", () => {\n  it(\"always renders two decimals\", () => {\n    expect(formatConfidence(0.9)).toBe(\"0.90\");\n    expect(formatConfidence(1)).toBe(\"1.00\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/reviewer-label.ts` → `reviewerLabel`**\n```ts\n// lib/reviewer-label.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { reviewerLabel } from \"@/lib/reviewer-label\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewerLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"prefers username over email\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"j.rao\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to email when username is null\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"j@x.com\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to the fallback id when user is null\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel(null, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"user_123\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back when username is empty string\", () => {\n    // \"\" is falsy-but-not-null — ?? does NOT treat it as missing. Verify intended behavior.\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"\", primaryEmailAddress: null }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/uuid.ts` → `isUuid`**\n```ts\ndescribe(\"isUuid\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts a canonical v4 uuid\", () => expect(isUuid(\"a41fc9d2-1234-4abc-8def-0123456789ab\")).toBe(true));\n  it(\"is case-insensitive\", () => expect(isUuid(\"A41FC9D2-1234-4ABC-8DEF-0123456789AB\")).toBe(true));\n  it.each([\"\", \"banana\", \"a41fc9d2\", \"a41fc9d2-1234-4abc-8def-0123456789ab-extra\", \"  a41fc9d2-1234-4abc-8def-0123456789ab  \"])(\n    \"rejects %s\",\n    (bad) => expect(isUuid(bad)).toBe(false),\n  );\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/validate-value.ts`** — the richest pure-logic file, and the one guarding a security-adjacent invariant (\"no hallucinated value written\").\n```ts\n// lib/validate-value.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues } from \"@/lib/validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"lowercases and strips punctuation\", () => expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(\"acme\"));\n  it(\"strips a single legal suffix\", () => expect(foldValue(\"Acme Inc.\")).toBe(\"acme\"));\n  it(\"strips compound suffixes longest-first (Pvt Ltd)\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n  it(\"does not strip a suffix that IS the whole value\", () => expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).toBe(\"ltd\"));\n  it(\"collapses internal whitespace\", () => expect(foldValue(\"Acme   Inc\")).toBe(\"acme\"));\n  it(\"normalizes unicode (NFKD)\", () => expect(foldValue(\"Ácme\")).toBe(\"acme\"));\n  it(\"handles empty string\", () => expect(foldValue(\"\")).toBe(\"\"));\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  const observed = [\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\"];\n  it(\"accepts an exact match\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"ACC-4417\", observed)).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACC-4417\" });\n  });\n  it(\"accepts a folded/normalized match\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"acc 4417\", [\"Acme Inc.\"])).toEqual(expect.objectContaining({ ok: true }));\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an invented value not present on either side\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"ACC-9999\", observed);\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects empty/whitespace-only input\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"   \", observed).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"reports 'nothing to choose from' when both observed values are blank\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"anything\", [\"\", \"  \"]);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, reason: expect.stringContaining(\"Neither side\") });\n  });\n  it(\"trims candidate before comparing\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"  ACC-4417  \", observed)).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACC-4417\" });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"flattens both sides and drops blanks\", () => {\n    expect(observedValues({ a: { values: [\"X\", \"\"] }, b: { values: [\"Y\"] } })).toEqual([\"X\", \"Y\"]);\n  });\n  it(\"returns empty array when both sides are empty (orphan/orphan edge case)\", () => {\n    expect(observedValues({ a: { values: [] }, b: { values: [] } })).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/rule-trace.ts` → `deriveRuleTrace`** — 4 distinct branches (unresolved / rule-decided / agent-proposed / escalated-no-value), none tested.\n```ts\n// lib/rule-trace.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { deriveRuleTrace } from \"@/lib/rule-trace\";\n// build a minimal QueueRow fixture per case\n\ndescribe(\"deriveRuleTrace\", () => {\n  it(\"returns a single not-yet-resolved step when resolution is null\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"marks classify+apply as ran when a rule decided with a value\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"marks classify+propose as ran when no rule matched but a value was proposed\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"marks only classify as ran when a rule escalated (no value)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"validate.ran is true iff a value reached it, regardless of rule vs agent origin\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/audit-detail.ts`** — reads an open `Record<string, unknown>` bag; every branch is an untested edge case (wrong type in a key, missing key, `from === to`, etc.)\n```ts\ndescribe(\"auditDetailParts\", () => {\n  it(\"ignores keys of the wrong type (e.g. confidence as a string)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"collapses from→to to just 'to' when from is missing\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"omits the arrow when from === to\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns [] for a detail object with no recognized keys\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"picks the right count noun per AuditAction\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"renders 'was <status>' with underscores replaced by hyphens\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\ndescribe(\"auditDetailLine\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null (not empty string) when there are no parts\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "2. Derived logic in `types/*.ts`",
        "content": "\n**`types/run.ts`** — `isTerminalRunStatus`, `runStageIndex`, `isStatKnown`, `failedStage`.\n```ts\ndescribe(\"failedStage\", () => {\n  it(\"parses 'stage=extract' from a free-text error\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"EngineDispatch: timeout\\nstage=dispatch\")).toBe(\"queued\");\n  });\n  it(\"returns null when the error has no stage= marker\", () => expect(failedStage(\"boom\")).toBeNull());\n  it(\"returns null for a null error\", () => expect(failedStage(null)).toBeNull());\n  it(\"is case-insensitive on the stage verb\", () => expect(failedStage(\"STAGE=EXTRACT\")).toBe(\"extracting\"));\n  it(\"returns null for an unrecognized stage verb\", () => expect(failedStage(\"stage=teleport\")).toBeNull());\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isStatKnown\", () => {\n  it(\"is true for every stat once status is complete\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"is true for every stat once status is failed (can't know which it reached)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"is false for a stat whose producing stage hasn't finished yet\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"extracting\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"is true once the producing stage is strictly behind current\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"entitiesA\", \"matching\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"runStageIndex / isTerminalRunStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"returns -1 for 'failed' (not a stage)\", () => expect(runStageIndex(\"failed\")).toBe(-1));\n  it(\"terminal only for complete and failed\", () => {\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"resolving\")).toBe(false);\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"complete\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"failed\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`types/rules.ts`** — `ruleSpecificity`, `orderRulesByEvaluation` (a stable sort — easy to silently break).\n```ts\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  it.each([\n    [{ field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" }, 0],\n    [{ field: \"name\", entityType: \"*\" }, 2],\n    [{ field: \"*\", entityType: \"account\" }, 1],\n    [{ field: \"name\", entityType: \"account\" }, 3],\n  ])(\"%o -> %i\", (partial, expected) => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ ...baseRule, ...partial })).toBe(expected);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"orderRulesByEvaluation\", () => {\n  it(\"sorts most specific first\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"preserves author order for ties (stable sort)\", () => {\n    // two rules with identical specificity — assert original relative order survives\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`types/queue.ts`** — `conflictFieldLabel`, `severityReason`, plus the `queueQuerySchema` transform (comma-separated severities → filtered numeric array — this silently drops invalid values, worth locking down).\n```ts\ndescribe(\"conflictFieldLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"returns 'entity absent' for orphan regardless of field\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns 'N → M' for a duplicate that collapsed record count\", () => {\n    expect(conflictFieldLabel({ field: \"x\", conflictClass: \"duplicate\", a: { values: [\"1\",\"2\"], present: true }, b: { values: [\"1\"], present: true } })).toBe(\"2 → 1\");\n  });\n  it(\"returns 'duplicate record' when duplicate counts are equal or one side is empty\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns the raw field name for structural/attribute/cosmetic\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"queueQuerySchema\", () => {\n  it(\"defaults status to 'escalated' and view to 'ledger' when absent\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"parses 'sev=4,3' into [4,3]\", () => {\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.parse({ severities: \"4,3\" }).severities).toEqual([4, 3]);\n  });\n  it(\"silently drops out-of-range severities instead of rejecting the request\", () => {\n    // documents current (permissive) behavior — flag if unintended\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.parse({ severities: \"4,9,abc\" }).severities).toEqual([4]);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects page < 1\", () => expect(() => queueQuerySchema.parse({ page: 0 })).not.toThrow()); // coerced default — verify actual behavior\n  it(\"rejects a field longer than 80 chars\", () => {\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.safeParse({ field: \"x\".repeat(81) }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`types/resolution.ts` → `isHumanDecided`**, and the `reviewActionSchema` discriminated union:\n```ts\ndescribe(\"reviewActionSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts approve/reject without overrideValue\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"requires a non-empty overrideValue when action is override\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\", overrideValue: \"\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an unknown action literal\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"delete\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"truncates/rejects a note over 500 chars\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n**`types/rules.ts` → `survivorshipRuleSchema` refine**: no test that `prefer_source` without `preferredSourceId` is actually rejected — this is the one custom `.refine()` in the schema layer and currently unverified.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "3. `lib/api-client.ts` — needs `fetch` mocking",
        "content": "\nUntested: success path, non-OK response with/without `issues`, non-OK response with unparsable body, and **network failure** (the `catch` branch — currently the only place a user-facing \"check your connection\" message is produced).\n\n```ts\n// lib/api-client.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, afterEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { postJson, patchJson } from \"@/lib/api-client\";\n\nafterEach(() => vi.restoreAllMocks());\n\ndescribe(\"postJson / patchJson\", () => {\n  it(\"returns ok:true with parsed data on 2xx\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(JSON.stringify({ id: 1 }), { status: 200 })));\n    expect(await postJson(\"/api/x\", {})).toEqual({ ok: true, data: { id: 1 } });\n  });\n\n  it(\"surfaces server error message + field issues on 400\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(\n      new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: \"Invalid\", issues: { field: \"required\" } }), { status: 400 }),\n    ));\n    expect(await postJson(\"/api/x\", {})).toEqual({ ok: false, message: \"Invalid\", issues: { field: \"required\" } });\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to a generic message when the error body has no 'error' field\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"{}\", { status: 500 })));\n    expect((await postJson(\"/api/x\", {})).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles a non-JSON error body without throwing\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"<html>502</html>\", { status: 502 })));\n    const result = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns a connectivity message when fetch itself throws\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new TypeError(\"Failed to fetch\")));\n    expect(await postJson(\"/api/x\", {})).toEqual({ ok: false, message: expect.stringContaining(\"Could not reach\") });\n  });\n\n  it(\"uses PATCH method for patchJson\", async () => {\n    const fetchMock = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"{}\", { status: 200 }));\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", fetchMock);\n    await patchJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(fetchMock).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\"/api/x\", expect.objectContaining({ method: \"PATCH\" }));\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "4. `components/conflicts/use-review.ts` — the one client hook",
        "content": "\nNeeds `@testing-library/react` + a mocked `next/navigation` router + mocked `patchJson`. Untested behavior: pending-state toggling, optimistic `decided` map update, error path leaving state untouched, and that `router.refresh()` fires only on success.\n\n```ts\n// components/conflicts/use-review.test.tsx\n// @vitest-environment jsdom\nimport { renderHook, act, waitFor } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { useReview } from \"@/components/conflicts/use-review\";\n\nconst refresh = vi.fn();\nvi.mock(\"next/navigation\", () => ({ useRouter: () => ({ refresh }) }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/api-client\", () => ({ patchJson: vi.fn() }));\n\nimport { patchJson } from \"@/lib/api-client\";\n\nbeforeEach(() => { refresh.mockClear(); vi.mocked(patchJson).mockReset(); });\n\ndescribe(\"useReview\", () => {\n  it(\"sets pendingId during the request and clears it after\", async () => { /* assert pendingId transitions */ });\n\n  it(\"records the server's status/reviewedBy in `decided` on success\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(patchJson).mockResolvedValue({ ok: true, data: { conflictId: \"c1\", status: \"approved\", reviewedBy: \"j.rao\" } });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n    await act(async () => { await result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"approve\" }); });\n    expect(result.current.decided.c1).toEqual({ status: \"approved\", reviewedBy: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"calls router.refresh() only after a successful submit\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(patchJson).mockResolvedValue({ ok: true, data: { conflictId: \"c1\", status: \"approved\", reviewedBy: \"j\" } });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n    await act(async () => { await result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"approve\" }); });\n    expect(refresh).toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it(\"leaves `decided` untouched and does NOT refresh on failure\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(patchJson).mockResolvedValue({ ok: false, message: \"conflict already resolved\" });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n    const outcome = await act(async () => result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"approve\" }));\n    expect(outcome).toEqual({ ok: false, message: \"conflict already resolved\" });\n    expect(result.current.decided.c1).toBeUndefined();\n    expect(refresh).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not let a second submit for a different conflict clobber the first entry\", async () => { /* map-merge regression guard */ });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "5. `lib/server/*.ts` — DB-backed, currently entirely untested",
        "content": "\nEvery function in `audit.ts`, `auth.ts`, `conflicts.ts`, `engine.ts`, `entities.ts`, `export.ts`, `rulesets.ts`, `runs.ts`, `sources.ts` is untested. Two viable strategies, not mutually exclusive:\n\n- **Unit-mock `getDb()`** (`vi.mock(\"@/lib/db\")`) for functions whose logic is worth isolating from Postgres — e.g. `toQueueRow`'s presence/side-labeling logic in `conflicts.ts`, `appliedValue`/`applyDecisions` in `export.ts`, `csvCell`/`decisionsToCsv` in `export.ts`. These have real branching logic independent of the query.\n- **Integration tests against a real ephemeral Postgres** (Testcontainers, or a `docker compose` test DB + drizzle migrations) for anything that composes a Drizzle query chain — mocking `.select().from().innerJoin().where().orderBy().limit()` by hand is brittle and tests the mock, not the code.\n\nHighest-value untested logic, regardless of harness chosen:\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/conflicts.test.ts — pure-ish branch inside toQueueRow, extract if needed for unit testing\ndescribe(\"toQueueRow presence logic\", () => {\n  it(\"marks an orphan's absent side present:false when its values are empty\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"files an orphan under whichever side actually holds the record\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"labels sourceName 'unknown source' when the entity's sourceId matches neither run source (engine-bug guard)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\n// lib/server/conflicts.test.ts — recordReview, the highest-risk function in the app\ndescribe(\"recordReview\", () => {\n  it(\"returns 404 when the conflict does not exist\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns 409 when the conflict has no resolution yet (run still resolving)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns 409 on 'approve' when proposedValue is empty (escalated, nothing to approve)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"rejects an override value not among the observed values (400)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"stores the folded/normalized match, not the typed override text\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"clears overrideValue when moving off a previous override to approve/reject\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"never writes reviewedBy from anything but the passed-in Reviewer\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"appends exactly one audit_log row per call, with previousStatus set\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\n// lib/server/export.ts\ndescribe(\"decisionsToCsv\", () => {\n  it(\"quotes cells containing commas, quotes, or newlines\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"escapes an embedded double-quote by doubling it\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"renders null as an empty cell, not the string 'null'\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"ends the file with \\\\r\\\\n, including when there are zero rows\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\ndescribe(\"appliedValue\", () => {\n  it.each([\"auto_applied\", \"approved\", \"overridden\"])(\"returns a value when status is %s\", (s) => { /* ... */ });\n  it.each([\"proposed\", \"escalated\", \"rejected\", null])(\"returns null for %s\", (s) => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns overrideValue (not proposedValue) specifically for 'overridden'\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\ndescribe(\"applyDecisions\", () => {\n  it(\"marks reparented:true only when the resolved parent differs from the original\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"ignores decisions for fields other than parentExternalId\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\ndescribe(\"estimateExportBytes\", () => {\n  it(\"sums only the requested sections, ignoring sizing for unselected ones\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\n// lib/server/rulesets.ts\ndescribe(\"createRulesetVersion\", () => {\n  it(\"assigns version = highest existing + 1 for the same name\", async () => { /* integration */ });\n  it(\"starts a brand-new policy name at version 1\", async () => { /* integration */ });\n  it(\"deactivates every other ruleset when activating the new one (exactly one active)\", async () => { /* integration */ });\n  it(\"two concurrent saves of the same name do not both get the same version (advisory lock)\", async () => {\n    // integration-only: fire two createRulesetVersion calls concurrently, assert distinct versions\n  });\n});\n\n// lib/server/auth.ts\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"throws when there is no authenticated session\", async () => { /* mock @clerk/nextjs/server */ });\n  it(\"prefers username, falling back through reviewerLabel\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\n// lib/server/engine.ts\ndescribe(\"startRun\", () => {\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError when ENGINE_URL is unset\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError on a non-OK response, including status+body\", async () => { /* mock fetch */ });\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError when the engine returns 200 with a body that fails schema validation\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError with 'no response within Ns' on an AbortSignal timeout\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\ndescribe(\"fetchEngineStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null (not throw) when the engine is unreachable\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"returns null when the engine's response fails schema validation\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "6. `app/api/**/route.ts` — no integration tests at all",
        "content": "\nNone of the 9 route handlers are tested. Each is a thin Zod-validate → server-call → shape-response layer, but several have branching worth locking down:\n\n```ts\n// app/api/runs/route.test.ts — POST /api/runs\ndescribe(\"POST /api/runs\", () => {\n  it(\"400s when sourceAId === sourceBId\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s 'Source A no longer exists' when sourceAId isn't found, even if body is otherwise valid\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s when the ruleset id no longer exists\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"still returns 201 with the run id when the engine dispatch fails, and records run_failed audit\", async () => {\n    // mock startRun to throw EngineUnreachableError; assert failUndispatchedRun + appendAudit called, response is 201\n  });\n  it(\"rethrows a non-EngineUnreachableError from startRun rather than swallowing it\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s with field-level issues when body fails createRunSchema\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\n// app/api/conflicts/[conflictId]/resolution/route.test.ts\ndescribe(\"PATCH /api/conflicts/:conflictId/resolution\", () => {\n  it(\"404s immediately for a non-UUID conflictId, without touching the DB\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"maps recordReview's {ok:false, code} straight through to the response status\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"never accepts a reviewedBy field from the request body (ignored even if present)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\n// app/api/runs/[runId]/export/route.test.ts\ndescribe(\"GET /api/runs/:runId/export\", () => {\n  it(\"defaults to sections=hierarchy,decisions when ?sections is absent\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s on an unknown section name\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"de-duplicates and canonically orders sections regardless of query order\", async () => {\n    // ?sections=stats,hierarchy,hierarchy -> canonical order, deduped\n  });\n  it(\"400s on format other than json/csv\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"CSV response omits hierarchy/orphans/stats even if requested\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"sets content-disposition filename from shortRunId with the interpunct stripped\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\n// app/api/audit/export/route.test.ts\ndescribe(\"GET /api/audit/export\", () => {\n  it(\"404s when runId is a well-formed UUID but no such run exists\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"400s on an invalid `action` query param\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"omits the runId filter entirely when not provided (exports everything)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n\n// app/api/_lib/respond.test.ts\ndescribe(\"parseJson\", () => {\n  it(\"400s with 'Body must be JSON.' when the body isn't valid JSON\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"maps each Zod issue to its dotted path in `issues`, using '_' for root-level issues\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "7. `proxy.ts` — auth middleware, untested",
        "content": "\n```ts\ndescribe(\"isPublicRoute matcher\", () => {\n  it(\"treats / and /sign-in* and /sign-up* as public\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"requires auth for every other page and every /api/* and /trpc/* route\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"excludes static assets per the config.matcher pattern (css/js/images/fonts/csv/office docs)\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\nThis is small but security-relevant — a regex/matcher regression here silently exposes an internal console. Worth a dedicated test even if the middleware body itself is one line, since `clerkMiddleware` mocking is the only way to catch a bad matcher before it ships.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Missing error-handling coverage, called out specifically",
        "content": "\n- `lib/server/engine.ts`: timeout vs. generic network failure produce different messages (`describe()`) — untested branch.\n- `lib/api-client.ts`: unparsable JSON error body (`.catch(() => null)`) — untested.\n- `app/api/runs/route.ts`: the only place that distinguishes \"engine dispatch failed\" (soft failure, 201 + failed run) from \"everything else\" (rethrow) — untested, and it's the one route with real error-recovery logic.\n- `lib/server/rulesets.ts`: the advisory-lock concurrency guard against two simultaneous \"save as vN\" — currently has no test proving it actually prevents a duplicate version number.\n- `lib/server/conflicts.ts` `recordReview`: three distinct rejection codes (400/404/409) with different triggering conditions — none tested.\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Integration test gaps",
        "content": "- End-to-end review flow: create a run → seed a conflict/resolution → PATCH override with an invalid value (expect 400, no audit row written) → PATCH override with a valid value (expect 200, resolutions row updated, exactly one audit_log row appended). Nothing currently proves the DB write and the audit append are consistent with each other.\n- Export round-trip: run with mixed escalated/auto-applied/overridden resolutions → JSON export → CSV export → assert both agree on `appliedValue` for the same conflict.\n- Auth boundary: an unauthenticated request to any `/api/*` route is rejected by `proxy.ts` before reaching the handler (currently only implied by code inspection, never exercised).\n- Ruleset versioning reproducibility: a run created under ruleset v3, then v4 is saved — assert the run's queue rows still resolve `appliedRuleStrategy` from v3, not v4 (`ruleStrategies()` in `conflicts.ts` reads from the run's own ruleset version, and there's no test proving old runs don't silently relabel).\n\n---\n\n**One aside, unrelated to coverage but worth flagging**: your working directory root has a couple of stray zero-byte files that look like broken shell-redirect artifacts — `String(n).padStart(2` and `r.conflictClass` — plus git status shows deleted `.env.example` and `rule.strategy` and an untracked `,` file. I didn't touch any of these since they're outside this task's scope, but you may want to clean them up separately.",
        "level": 3
      }
    ],
